# decode_invalid_utf8_reject.tkr — the SM-STRU32 codec fixture. `main.tks` feeds
# `teko::text::decode_utf8_u32` an overlong 2-byte encoding of NUL (`0xC0 0x80`, ill-formed per
# RFC 3629) and exits 0 only if the call returns `error` (never a fabricated codepoint).

Feature: decode_invalid_utf8_reject — decode_utf8_u32 rejects ill-formed UTF-8

  Scenario: overlong_two_byte_nul_is_rejected
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 0
